course: dictionary
lesson: 6897
title: Overwhelm: too much at once
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To overwhelm someone is to give them so much of a feeling, or so much to do, that they cannot cope. Overwhelm is a verb, so it changes: overwhelms, overwhelmed, overwhelming. «Teenagers sometimes run off when they feel overwhelmed» tells you the feeling is too big to manage, so they may act without thinking.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. The sentence says grown-ups and the police help find them, so feeling overwhelmed can happen to anyone, and help is there. Feeling overwhelmed is normal. You can cope with it by breaking the task into small steps and talking to someone you trust.
explain: The word has other meanings too. An army can overwhelm its enemy, which means beat them completely with greater force. A flood can overwhelm a village, which means cover it completely. Check the sentence to see which meaning fits.
fact: To overwhelm means to give someone so much of a feeling or task that they cannot cope.
fact: «Overwhelmed» means feeling that there is too much to deal with.
fact: Feeling overwhelmed is normal, and breaking a task into small steps can help.
fact: To overwhelm an enemy means to beat it completely with greater force.
fact: To overwhelm can also mean to cover something completely, like a flood.
exercise: «Teenagers sometimes run off when they feel overwhelmed.» What does overwhelmed mean here? | Feeling very cheerful and bright | Running very fast | *Having so much to deal with that you cannot cope | Feeling cold and wet
exercise: The stronger army began to overwhelm the enemy. What does overwhelm mean here? | Count them carefully | Make friends with them | Hide from them | *Beat them completely with greater force
exercise: Maya feels overwhelmed by her long list of jobs. Which step could help her? | *Break the jobs into small steps and talk to someone | Add more jobs to the list | Hide under the bed for the rest of the day | Ignore the list and hope it goes away
test: The flood water began to overwhelm the low fields. What does overwhelm mean? | Make smaller | *Cover completely | Dry up slowly | Freeze solid
test: Yesterday Ben felt ___ by all the noise. Which form fits? | Overwhelm | *Overwhelmed | Overwhelms | Overwhelming
exam: Which sentence uses overwhelm to mean cover completely? | *The flood began to overwhelm the streets | The sun began to shine on the streets | The dog began to sleep in the streets | The children began to sing in the streets
